  - path: docs/decisions/dec-32-body-is-the-main-zone.html
    tier: T2
    action: added
    distills: "The owner's round as a standing rule, opened under the distillation checklist's 'non-obvious choice made or reversed' row because it reverses three lines of a closed design: a detail panel never scrolls as a whole; the body is its main zone (flex-1, scrolls inside); every other zone is bounded (headers at natural height up to 35% of the panel, scrolling inside, heading naming the count; identity row and flow line chrome); a screen-tall value is clamped to three lines with more/less under its name — a named, reversible view under display-equals-payload, not a truncation; a scroll container holding a display:contents grid is positioned, because WebKit leaks its overflow into the document otherwise. Rejected alternatives with reasons (one scroll region, tabs, ellipsis, a pixel cap, positioning alone) and the consequences forced on FlowDetail, KeyValueRow, Section, BodyViewer and any later detail screen. Two tokens (value-clamp; a declared maxHeight scale with zone-cap)."
